1
00:00:01,141 --> 00:00:07,411
(The 1st Rainbow Summer Retreat)

2
00:00:07,641 --> 00:00:08,680
- Here. - It's smooth here.

3
00:00:08,681 --> 00:00:11,151
Razor blades don't work on me now.

4
00:00:12,181 --> 00:00:13,880
- Nine more people have to come. - Hello.

5
00:00:13,881 --> 00:00:14,980
- My gosh. - Hey.

6
00:00:14,981 --> 00:00:16,820
- Hello. - Why did you bring so much stuff?

7
00:00:16,821 --> 00:00:17,851
I know, right?

8
00:00:18,151 --> 00:00:20,091
- Hello. - I can tell this is bread.

9
00:00:20,191 --> 00:00:21,890
It is. I wanted to share it with everyone on our way there.

10
00:00:21,891 --> 00:00:22,931
I bet it's going to taste good.

11
00:00:24,091 --> 00:00:27,160
(The 1st Rainbow Summer Retreat was announced last week.)

12
00:00:27,161 --> 00:00:28,400
(Newsletter: The 2026 Rainbow Summer Retreat)

13
00:00:28,401 --> 00:00:30,570
(It's been a while since I got anything printed on the pulp paper.)

14
00:00:30,571 --> 00:00:34,101
(It brought old memories of my school retreats.)

15
00:00:34,971 --> 00:00:37,570
(They will stay in a youth hostel in Suwon.)

16
00:00:37,571 --> 00:00:39,071
(Happy to hear the news)

17
00:00:39,841 --> 00:00:43,381
(Make sure to show up by 10am.)

18
00:00:43,581 --> 00:00:45,110
- Have you been well? - Hey.

19
00:00:45,111 --> 00:00:46,350
(Today is the day of the summer retreat.)

20
00:00:46,351 --> 00:00:47,781
- There are four of us now. - Yes.

21
00:00:49,351 --> 00:00:50,720
- My gosh. - Hello.

22
00:00:50,721 --> 00:00:52,191
- You're here. - Nice to see you, everyone.

23
00:00:53,091 --> 00:00:56,890
(Hello.)

24
00:00:56,891 --> 00:00:57,991
He said hello five times.

25
00:00:59,531 --> 00:01:01,360
- It was so awkward then. Right? - Nice to meet you.

26
00:01:01,361 --> 00:01:02,501
- I'm Seo Bum June. - It was so awkward.

27
00:01:02,801 --> 00:01:03,830
- Hello. - Nice to meet you.

28
00:01:03,831 --> 00:01:05,701
- I'm Seo Bum June. - You guys have never met before?

29
00:01:05,901 --> 00:01:07,040
- It's our first time meeting. - Yes.

30
00:01:07,041 --> 00:01:08,241
- They've never met before. - I see.

31
00:01:08,301 --> 00:01:10,671
Do you know who these two guys are?

32
00:01:11,441 --> 00:01:13,311
- They're actors, right? - Yes.

33
00:01:13,781 --> 00:01:14,940
- "Actors." - And you are...

34
00:01:14,941 --> 00:01:16,550
- What's his name? - You are Bae Na Ra.

35
00:01:16,551 --> 00:01:18,451
- You're Seo Bum June. - My gosh.

36
00:01:18,651 --> 00:01:20,080
- I was nervous. - Name a project they're famous for.

37
00:01:20,081 --> 00:01:21,821
A project they're famous for? Well,

38
00:01:22,221 --> 00:01:23,650
- you were in that thing. - What?

39
00:01:23,651 --> 00:01:25,091
You were in that impressive action scene.

40
00:01:25,651 --> 00:01:27,090
- An impressive action scene. - What's the title?

41
00:01:27,091 --> 00:01:28,461
- The title? - It's "Impressive Action Scene?"

42
00:01:29,121 --> 00:01:30,130
"Weak Hero."

43
00:01:30,131 --> 00:01:31,160
(He remembers it.)

44
00:01:31,161 --> 00:01:32,161
You were in "Weak Hero."

45
00:01:32,162 --> 00:01:33,731
And don't you love bread?

46
00:01:34,331 --> 00:01:36,101
- You love bread. - Yes. And my famous project?

47
00:01:36,201 --> 00:01:37,730
Your famous project is I Live Alone.

48
00:01:37,731 --> 00:01:39,641
(The project he's famous for is I Live Alone?)

49
00:01:39,901 --> 00:01:41,170
- I'm sorry, Bum June. - I'm sorry.

50
00:01:41,171 --> 00:01:42,200
I'm sorry.

51
00:01:42,201 --> 00:01:43,610
- You need to work harder. - I'll work harder.

52
00:01:43,611 --> 00:01:44,770
(The actor with 2 Rookie Awards in 2024 is disappointed.)

53
00:01:44,771 --> 00:01:46,311
- I'll make sure to watch it. - Yes.

54
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:47,581
- Hello. - It's Dae Ho.

55
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:49,580
- Hello. - Hi.

56
00:01:49,581 --> 00:01:51,380
(The members are arriving one at a time.)

57
00:01:51,381 --> 00:01:52,751
- Hello. - Gosh.

58
00:01:53,681 --> 00:01:54,681
It's Park Gyeong Hye.

59
00:01:54,682 --> 00:01:55,920
- There are a lot of people. - It's so crowded.

60
00:01:55,921 --> 00:01:57,051
There are so many people.

61
00:01:57,591 --> 00:01:59,021
The fashionista is here.

62
00:01:59,191 --> 00:02:00,221
Right.

63
00:02:01,991 --> 00:02:02,991
Joy.

64
00:02:02,992 --> 00:02:04,430
(Joy and MINHO are the last ones to arrive.)

65
00:02:04,431 --> 00:02:05,491
MINHO.

66
00:02:05,761 --> 00:02:07,831
- Hello. - Hello.

67
00:02:07,931 --> 00:02:09,570
- Hey. This is crazy. - We were a big group.

68
00:02:09,571 --> 00:02:11,030
- It's so crowded. - He's so handsome.

69
00:02:11,031 --> 00:02:12,731
Hello. Yes. Nice to meet you.

70
00:02:14,901 --> 00:02:15,971
That was random.

71
00:02:16,941 --> 00:02:18,640
- What's going on? - There's more?

72
00:02:18,641 --> 00:02:19,641
- No way. - No way.

73
00:02:19,881 --> 00:02:21,281
- No way. - For real?

74
00:02:21,911 --> 00:02:23,211
Stop that.

75
00:02:26,851 --> 00:02:28,621
(Loving it)

76
00:02:29,151 --> 00:02:31,190
He was so cool!

77
00:02:31,191 --> 00:02:32,691
- That was so hip, right? - It was so cool.

78
00:02:33,161 --> 00:02:34,961
It was really cool.

79
00:02:35,761 --> 00:02:36,790
It's him!

80
00:02:36,791 --> 00:02:38,991
(Driver Ku, the designated driver of the retreat)

81
00:02:40,001 --> 00:02:42,761
(Amazed)

82
00:02:43,171 --> 00:02:44,901
(Cheering wholeheartedly)

83
00:02:45,271 --> 00:02:46,671
Make some noise!

84
00:02:47,301 --> 00:02:48,341
- Yes! - Let's go!

85
00:02:48,771 --> 00:02:50,740
Hey, get in!

86
00:02:50,741 --> 00:02:51,841
"Hey, get in."

87
00:02:52,611 --> 00:02:53,680
Gosh, for real?

88
00:02:53,681 --> 00:02:55,081
This is embarrassing.

89
00:02:55,541 --> 00:02:56,550
- That's so cool. - This is amazing.

90
00:02:56,551 --> 00:02:57,551
Sir!

91
00:02:57,552 --> 00:02:59,650
(You just trust me.)

92
00:02:59,651 --> 00:03:00,950
- That's cool. - It's so funny.

93
00:03:00,951 --> 00:03:02,620
Come on in. Wait. Let me park it.

94
00:03:02,621 --> 00:03:03,950
- Give me a second. - Academy bus drivers...

95
00:03:03,951 --> 00:03:05,320
looked just like him back in my day.

96
00:03:05,321 --> 00:03:06,690
- He also wore gloves. - Yes, the gloves.

97
00:03:06,691 --> 00:03:07,821
- He was very detailed. - Yes.

98
00:03:08,391 --> 00:03:10,031
All right. Don't act cheeky now.

99
00:03:10,291 --> 00:03:11,430
- Drive safely. - It's not easy to drive a van.

100
00:03:11,431 --> 00:03:12,531
I've tried it once.

101
00:03:13,161 --> 00:03:14,500
- Do you need help? - Gosh, no. It's heavy.

102
00:03:14,501 --> 00:03:16,101
- No. - Gosh.

103
00:03:16,471 --> 00:03:18,470
(Grabbing)

104
00:03:18,471 --> 00:03:19,940
- My gosh. Oh, no. - No. It's light.

105
00:03:19,941 --> 00:03:20,941
Let me help you.

106
00:03:20,942 --> 00:03:22,471
- Seon Min, that was cool. - That was Seon Min.

107
00:03:23,271 --> 00:03:25,411
(What was that? That was pretty cool.)

108
00:03:25,711 --> 00:03:27,511
Well, I think it's basic etiquette.

109
00:03:27,781 --> 00:03:28,810
"Etiquette?"

110
00:03:28,811 --> 00:03:30,211
(Laughing)

111
00:03:30,481 --> 00:03:31,651
- Your bags... - We can put them in here, right?

112
00:03:31,781 --> 00:03:33,850
Carefully load them in the trunk one at a time.

113
00:03:33,851 --> 00:03:35,451
I know, right? Bum June.

114
00:03:37,091 --> 00:03:38,491
All right. Get in.

115
00:03:38,891 --> 00:03:41,491
- I should sit here. - I wasn't there.

116
00:03:41,861 --> 00:03:43,131
- You were getting ready for it. - I was hosting my radio show.

117
00:03:43,661 --> 00:03:45,090
I'll make sure you all get in safely.

118
00:03:45,091 --> 00:03:46,300
(I'll see everyone get in.)

119
00:03:46,301 --> 00:03:48,531
- You're like a professional driver. - Gosh.

120
00:03:49,231 --> 00:03:50,371
Don't you worry about it.

121
00:03:50,501 --> 00:03:52,500
I have the Class One license to drive large vehicles.

122
00:03:52,501 --> 00:03:53,501
- Really? - Yes.

123
00:03:53,502 --> 00:03:54,570
- You do? - Yes.

124
00:03:54,571 --> 00:03:55,770
- Are you a good driver? - Come on, Hyun Moo.

125
00:03:55,771 --> 00:03:57,570
My nickname is Mad Max.

126
00:03:57,571 --> 00:03:58,640
- Mad Max? - Yes.

127
00:03:58,641 --> 00:03:59,780
It must be dangerous then.

128
00:03:59,781 --> 00:04:00,840
(What a nickname.)

129
00:04:00,841 --> 00:04:01,910
Seat belts. Are you all settled in?

130
00:04:01,911 --> 00:04:02,911
- Yes. - Yes.

131
00:04:02,912 --> 00:04:05,180
- We're not leaving anyone behind. - Okay.

132
00:04:05,181 --> 00:04:06,480
I'll close the door for you.

133
00:04:06,481 --> 00:04:07,681
(I'll close the door for you.)

134
00:04:08,581 --> 00:04:09,581
Let's go.

135
00:04:10,321 --> 00:04:11,390
I like this.

136
00:04:11,391 --> 00:04:12,721
- Gosh, thank you. - Really?

137
00:04:13,821 --> 00:04:15,860
I brought rice cakes. Have some rice cakes.

138
00:04:15,861 --> 00:04:17,861
- She bought rice cakes. - Oh, my.

139
00:04:18,331 --> 00:04:19,961
- She bought rice cakes. - Thank you!

140
00:04:20,331 --> 00:04:21,560
- My gosh. - They were really good.

141
00:04:21,561 --> 00:04:23,031
- My gosh. Thank you. - Here.

142
00:04:23,201 --> 00:04:25,701
I also bought bread on my way here.

143
00:04:25,971 --> 00:04:27,741
- My gosh. - Pass it up.

144
00:04:27,801 --> 00:04:30,041
- They're chosen by Bum June. - Thank you, Bum June.

145
00:04:30,171 --> 00:04:32,371
- They're chosen by Bum June. - That's amazing.

146
00:04:32,671 --> 00:04:34,041
This is a palate cleanser.

147
00:04:34,381 --> 00:04:35,740
(Seon Min also shares Shinbi peaches.)

148
00:04:35,741 --> 00:04:36,851
Shinbi peaches!

149
00:04:37,381 --> 00:04:38,410
They were good, right?

150
00:04:38,411 --> 00:04:40,080
My father runs a small peach farm.

151
00:04:40,081 --> 00:04:41,151
- Really? - Yes.

152
00:04:41,281 --> 00:04:43,120
- They were so good. - But I'm sorry.

153
00:04:43,121 --> 00:04:44,620
The season is over. I can get more next year.

154
00:04:44,621 --> 00:04:46,590
I already bought 5kg of those peaches.

155
00:04:46,591 --> 00:04:48,190
- Really? - Do you sell fruit?

156
00:04:48,191 --> 00:04:50,260
(What on earth?)

157
00:04:50,261 --> 00:04:52,231
- This is sulbbang. - It's sulbbang?

158
00:04:52,431 --> 00:04:54,361
- I washed everything. Have one. - We don't need to eat breakfast.

159
00:04:54,431 --> 00:04:57,430
Seeing how Bum June bought this, this must be the best tart now.

160
00:04:57,431 --> 00:04:59,130
- Right. - I should've skipped my radio show.

161
00:04:59,131 --> 00:05:00,170
(Joking)

162
00:05:00,171 --> 00:05:02,070
- I should've done that. - Because of the bread?

163
00:05:02,071 --> 00:05:03,771
Because of the bread, rice cakes, and fruit?

164
00:05:04,041 --> 00:05:05,340
Please drive safely.

165
00:05:05,341 --> 00:05:06,980
My gosh, don't worry. My nickname is Mad Max.

166
00:05:06,981 --> 00:05:08,340
- Don't worry. - Great.

167
00:05:08,341 --> 00:05:10,450
- Let's go. - My gosh.

168
00:05:10,451 --> 00:05:12,181
(They finally set out on their summer retreat.)

169
00:05:15,821 --> 00:05:18,251
(Back in the day, the bus rides to the retreat were full of fun.)

170
00:05:19,221 --> 00:05:20,361
That was the old days.

171
00:05:20,891 --> 00:05:22,121
That was the school retreat.

172
00:05:24,631 --> 00:05:26,360
Right. Pillow fights are fun.

173
00:05:26,361 --> 00:05:27,661
Right, pillow fights.

174
00:05:29,231 --> 00:05:33,601
(It was even more joyful with friends.)

175
00:05:35,341 --> 00:05:38,110
It's "Pebble Love" by Seo Min Ho.

176
00:05:38,111 --> 00:05:39,370
That's not the title.

177
00:05:39,371 --> 00:05:41,780
"Pebble Love?" My gosh. I haven't heard that in a while.

178
00:05:41,781 --> 00:05:42,911
I loved the playlist.

179
00:05:44,381 --> 00:05:50,051
(Romance is long gone, and only trot songs fill the air.)

180
00:05:50,791 --> 00:05:52,020
I bet CODE KUNST is getting inspired a lot today.

181
00:05:52,021 --> 00:05:53,560
(I bet CODE KUNST is getting inspired a lot today.)

182
00:05:53,561 --> 00:05:55,191
I bet he can write new songs right away.

183
00:05:57,631 --> 00:05:59,431
- Do you still exercise these days? - These days?

184
00:05:59,801 --> 00:06:01,461
- You run, right? - I do.

185
00:06:01,961 --> 00:06:03,731
Running is the easiest for me.

186
00:06:04,331 --> 00:06:05,731
It's the safest, right?

187
00:06:06,331 --> 00:06:08,301
(Turning back)

188
00:06:08,401 --> 00:06:09,940
Do you still run a lot?

189
00:06:09,941 --> 00:06:12,511
- You run every day, right? - Yes. I run a lot.

190
00:06:12,711 --> 00:06:15,540
- I watched a lot of your clips. - I see.

191
00:06:15,541 --> 00:06:17,151
I saw you exercise in those clips.

192
00:06:17,251 --> 00:06:20,050
It was awkward, so I wanted to find some common ground.

193
00:06:20,051 --> 00:06:21,121
(Chuckling)

194
00:06:21,251 --> 00:06:22,381
Why don't we go for a run together?

195
00:06:23,121 --> 00:06:24,550
I can run at your pace.

196
00:06:24,551 --> 00:06:25,651
Don't worry about that.

197
00:06:26,521 --> 00:06:27,890
(Approaching again)

198
00:06:27,891 --> 00:06:29,621
- Kian84. - Yes?

199
00:06:30,031 --> 00:06:33,091
- I'm used to running by myself. - Okay.

200
00:06:33,231 --> 00:06:35,600
Sometimes, running gets boring.

201
00:06:35,601 --> 00:06:37,570
(What should I do?)

202
00:06:37,571 --> 00:06:40,241
You should run with MINHO. It gets better then.

203
00:06:40,541 --> 00:06:42,000
- It reminded me of college days. - Okay.

204
00:06:42,001 --> 00:06:45,070
At orientation trips, some kids would start conversations...

205
00:06:45,071 --> 00:06:46,340
- Right. - to get to know each other.

206
00:06:46,341 --> 00:06:48,611
- Exactly. - He kept talking to everyone.

207
00:06:48,981 --> 00:06:52,411
I'll think about what kind of run we can do together.

208
00:06:52,651 --> 00:06:53,821
- That sounds good. - So...

209
00:06:53,951 --> 00:06:55,220
This was my first time today.

210
00:06:55,221 --> 00:06:56,791
- Things are awkward in the back. - My gosh.

211
00:06:56,891 --> 00:06:57,950
A talent show?

212
00:06:57,951 --> 00:06:59,751
(Feeling awkward)

213
00:06:59,991 --> 00:07:02,561
Do you typically stay quiet when you get in the car?

214
00:07:02,861 --> 00:07:05,931
I usually go to sleep because I get carsick.

215
00:07:06,131 --> 00:07:07,231
- Same here. - What about you?

216
00:07:07,701 --> 00:07:09,531
- I don't get shy around new people. - Okay.

217
00:07:10,031 --> 00:07:12,970
- But at first... - Are you just being careful?

218
00:07:12,971 --> 00:07:15,571
I might come across as rude. So I'm just being careful now.

219
00:07:15,671 --> 00:07:17,141
I don't know what to say now.

220
00:07:17,311 --> 00:07:18,941
I like this subtle awkwardness.

221
00:07:19,071 --> 00:07:20,340
- I like that too. - Me too.

222
00:07:20,341 --> 00:07:23,511
I rarely have occasions these days where I can feel that.

223
00:07:23,981 --> 00:07:26,521
(Treat me right when you have me)

224
00:07:26,851 --> 00:07:28,280
(Clueless of what's going on in the back,)

225
00:07:28,281 --> 00:07:29,720
(the guys in the front are just having fun.)

226
00:07:29,721 --> 00:07:31,250
Are you going to sing for the talent show?

227
00:07:31,251 --> 00:07:32,490
- What? - Will you sing?

228
00:07:32,491 --> 00:07:34,221
- Sing? Today? - For the talent show.

229
00:07:34,521 --> 00:07:35,591
It's a secret.

230
00:07:36,731 --> 00:07:39,091
- You should drop the honorifics. - Really?

231
00:07:39,831 --> 00:07:41,500
Please drop the honorifics with me too.

232
00:07:41,501 --> 00:07:42,561
Really?

233
00:07:42,761 --> 00:07:44,870
That's when you guys dropped the honorifics.

234
00:07:44,871 --> 00:07:47,801
Yes. They said we should drop the honorifics.

235
00:07:47,901 --> 00:07:50,040
How old is everyone? How old is Bum June?

236
00:07:50,041 --> 00:07:51,470
- They're around the same age. - Yes, we're around the same age.

237
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:53,171
We're 1 or 2 years apart.

238
00:07:53,681 --> 00:07:55,980
I have a hard time doing that. But let me try.

239
00:07:55,981 --> 00:07:57,111
(They are bonding as they drop the honorifics.)

240
00:07:57,851 --> 00:07:59,150
It's already funny.

241
00:07:59,151 --> 00:08:00,520
(The members are getting close to Suwon.)

242
00:08:00,521 --> 00:08:03,121
- It's giving youth hostel vibes. - We're in the suburbs.

243
00:08:05,021 --> 00:08:07,561
(A van drives along on a quiet road.)

244
00:08:07,961 --> 00:08:11,391
- Everyone, here's our youth hostel. - My gosh.

245
00:08:11,491 --> 00:08:13,031
(At last!)

246
00:08:13,231 --> 00:08:14,501
Gosh, a youth hostel.

247
00:08:14,831 --> 00:08:17,171
- No way. - They were the bomb back then.

248
00:08:17,431 --> 00:08:18,831
This place is really nice.

249
00:08:19,501 --> 00:08:21,740
- It's nice. - There's a podium too.

250
00:08:21,741 --> 00:08:22,841
Of course, there is.

251
00:08:23,841 --> 00:08:24,911
- No way. - My gosh.

252
00:08:25,771 --> 00:08:26,911
How nostalgic.

253
00:08:28,981 --> 00:08:30,911
It's our first summer retreat.

254
00:08:31,451 --> 00:08:35,681
(They arrive at the lush, green retreat venue.)

255
00:08:36,381 --> 00:08:37,721
Gosh, this place looks great.

256
00:08:38,621 --> 00:08:39,721
- No way. - My gosh.

257
00:08:39,891 --> 00:08:41,061
I love it.

